                                  "id": "1776901686951",
                                  "code": "GROUP_ITEM_DESCRIPTIONS_INTO_BUCKETS",
                                  "type": "LLM",
                                  "inputs": [
                                    {
                                      "id": "1776901686951_systemPrompt",
                                      "name": "systemPrompt",
                                      "type": "string",
                                      "value": ""
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "id": "1776901686951_prompt",
                                      "name": "prompt",
                                      "type": "string",
                                      "value": "### Instructions:\nProcess the provided object array using the following process. Use the itemDescription attribute from each object for consideration.\nGroup only items that refer to the exact same product/item and differ only by:\n- punctuation\n- capitalization\n- spacing\n- word order\n- abbreviations\n- minor typos\n- extra filler words\n\nDo NOT group items that are merely related by category, department, or use case.\nDo NOT group items that differ in size, model, brand, color, quantity, grade, material, or function.\nWhen uncertain, keep items separate.\nEach element in the array is an atomic string. Do NOT split strings on commas or any other special character.\n\nApply a conservative, deterministic grouping process:\n1. Normalize mentally for case, punctuation, spacing, and word order.\n2. Compare items pairwise for true equivalence.\n3. If A matches B and B matches C, all three must be in the same bucket.\n4. Use one canonical bucket name per group based on the simplest representative description.\n5. If multiple bucket names are possible, choose the first item in the bucket as the bucket label.\n\nEvery item description must appear in exactly one bucket.\nReturn only valid JSON in this format:\n{\n  \"buckets\": {\n    \"b1\": \"canonical bucket name\",\n    \"b2\": \"canonical bucket name\"\n  },\n  \"items\": {\n    \"original item description 1\": \"b1\",\n    \"original item description 2\": \"b1\",\n    \"original item description 3\": \"b2\"\n  }\n}\n\nUse the provided array exactly as given.\nReturn only valid JSON. No markdown. No code fences. No explanation.\n\n### Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.ITERATE_OVER_REQUISITION_BUS.ITERATE_OVER_REQUESTERS.ITERATE_OVER_SUPPLIERS.EXTRACT_ITEM_DESCRIPTIONS_FROM_REQUESTS.$output.result}} "
                                    }
                                  ],
                                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"buckets\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"items\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"buckets\",\n    \"items\"\n  ]\n}"
                                },
